  "result": "Done! I've implemented the payment tracking system for the invoicing module. Here's what was added:\n\n## Created `src/payments.js`\n\n- **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment on an invoice with validation:\n  - Only works on invoices with status `'issued'` or `'partially_paid'` (returns `NOT_ISSUED` error otherwise)\n  - Amount must be a positive integer in cents (returns `AMOUNT_INVALID` if not)\n  - Date must be valid YYYY-MM-DD format (returns `DATE_INVALID` if not)\n  - Cannot exceed the balance due (returns `OVERPAYMENT` if overpaying)\n  - Creates the payments array if missing, appends payment with `{ amount, date }`\n  - Updates status: `'paid'` when balance is fully covered, `'partially_paid'` while owed\n  - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` without mutating the original\n\n- **`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Returns total minus payments (clamped to 0)\n\n- **`totalPaid(invoice)`** \u2014 Sums all recorded payments\n\n## Updated `src/errors.js`\n\nAdded two new error codes:\n- `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 Can only record payments on issued or partially paid invoices\n- `OVERPAYMENT` \u2014 Payment amount exceeds the balance due\n\n## Created `test/payments.test.js`\n\n18 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Balance and payment calculations\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- All error cases and validations\n- Immutability of original invoice\n- Multiple payment accumulation\n\n**All 154 tests pass** (18 new + 136 existing).",
